rts them, with every edge","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"classified as a tree, back, forward or cross edge. Parallel edges are told apart: a repeated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tree edge is a forward edge at its own position. It holds a copy of the graph and can be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterated more than once. The search keeps its own stack, so a deep graph cannot overflow the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"call stack."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/traversal\/edgedepthfirstsearch","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearch","title":"EdgeDepthFirstSearch","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Traversal/documentation/Traversal":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"title":"Traversal","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/traversal","type":"topic"}}}